d members of the judiciary to  see if they would have the time  to to  assist with this kind of investigation  uh and i hope to be able to have more to  report on that in the very near future  thank you premier carolyn do you have a  follow-up  i do actually so um the review is one  thing what would the consequences be if  wrongdoing is found and why didn't you  just fire him  right away and then reinstate him if he  is cleared in some review  well i've looked at precedence such as  this where  uh you know when i was minister of  defense for example and we had a a  senior officer um with the serious  allegations made against them uh the  typical response would be to  put that person on a leave of absence uh  conduct an investigation  to determine the facts  and then to make a final decision about  their situation i think that is normal  in in a context like this let me say  this if  um chief mcphee  had alleged  that  he felt this was a interference in the  administration of justice the  independence of the police or  an effort to rescind the ticket if  i would have  made a uh immediate decision  uh  to remove mr maddie from cabinet but um  that's not the public statement that we  have  questions have been raised about  profiling i was not on this call  i was not  present at the time that this ticket was  issued  and i think given the issues that have  been raised  it is appropriate  to  allow for a little bit of time for an  investigation  from  somebody with  legal training who is impartial  to provide me with advice on uh whether  this constituted uh a uh an effort to  interfere in the independent  administration of justice so that's what  we're doing  as i said um i reached out to a number  of  nearly a dozen  senior former members of both  the judiciary and of government to get  their advice and that was the consensus  view of the people who who gave me  advice last monday and and i think it  again it's conventional with similar  circumstances that i've seen  thank you premier operator can you  please put through the next caller  still in short post media  hi there i'd like to go back to  children in hospital i know that they  still represent a smaller number than  their older counterparts but between  december 31st and yesterday it looks  like there were 160 admissions for  children under the age of 19. the same  time frame from last year was 35 so i  guess my question is  given the increase in the number of  children that are going to hospital with  clovis what's being done i guess to  protect this population especially given  the fact that they aren't eligible for a  booster shot yet  um  so perhaps dr hinshaw dr you  um  so perhaps dr hinshaw dr you  so i can speak to population protection  and i just want to make sure i  understand um so you're speaking about  the under five population or you're  speaking about the under 18 or i guess  it would be the under 12 population who  would be coming due for their second  doses in the next several weeks or or  all of them together just to clarify  yeah sorry i guess all of them together  but especially for the individuals that  haven't been able to get fully immunized  yet  so absolutely the number of children  currently in hospital as dr you  mentioned each of those children  would  have a significant impact on them and on  their family  and that should not be discounted  it is also true that the  percentage of cases that  are going to hospital when we look at  the evidence around the world about  omicron is a lower risk this is  unfortunately the consequence of the  significant transmission we're seeing  right now  it's absolutely critical that anyone who  is in a household with or interacts  regularly with someone who is in this  younger age group  receive their vaccines as soon as  possible it's clear that children who  live in a household  where all adults are fully immunized  have a lower risk of ending up in  hospital than children who live in a  household where not all adults are fully  immunized it's also true that those  children under one have the absolute  highest risk of all childhood age groups  and it's  really important that those who are  pregnant access the protection of  vaccine for themselves and for their  children  it's also critical again that all of us  do everything we can to minimize  transmission in the community so that we  can lower the chances of children being  exposed  but we do know again that  the higher numbers are due to the higher  transmission that we're seeing right now  and that protecting kids is really  something all of us can do together  the last time i looked at the data i  didn't see that any children with a  single dose of vaccine had been admitted  so even in that 5 to 11 year old age  group it's important to note that at  least the last time i checked we hadn't  seen  any  kids who were at least partially  vaccinated ending up in hospital it is  of course important for those children  to receive their booster and and most  who were early in the first dose will be  coming due for that very soon  so i encourage those parents to get  their kids fully vaccinated in that 5 to  11 year old age group but again it's  it's the vaccination of those around  them that is going to really be  important at minimizing risk  take your doctor and dylan do you have a  follow-up  yeah i do i'm not sure who this would be  directed towards but  in in recent weeks past months or so  we've seen the rollback of pcr testing  so children can't receive those if they  may have access to rapid tests through  their schools but many still do not  um  there's now no school outbreak reporting  um online at least officially  i'm hearing from a lot of parents if  they feel that they can't make safe  decisions for their children i would  like to get a response  to that to parents that feel that they  can't make an informed safe decision  on what's best for the children  we've been used to  having access to pcr testing for mild  illness in all age groups for almost two  years  and so it's really difficult when we've  been used to having that access when  we've been used to having  all of the outbreak data all of the case  data  the the shift that omicron has required  us to make is difficult especially over  a short time period so i sympathize with  parents who want the kind of information  they used to have  what is important to understand about  our current omicron wave is that  even though again our cases may be at a  plateau right now transmission is  incredibly high so if parents are trying  to decide what activities their children  should  engage in they need to understand that  there's a high likelihood  that there could be someone infectious  at almost any activity their children  participate in outside the home  which is exactly why in schools we've  ensured that there are additional levels  of protection with medical masks and  regular access to rapid testing for  asymptomatic screening in that context  and it is important for parents then to  understand they need to make the the  risk-based decisions that are  appropriate for their family based on  community spread at this time  because we simply  must use our access to testing for those  who need it for clinical reasons and for  those high-risk settings where the risk  of severe outcomes is very high such as  long-term care  thank you dr henshaw operator can you  please put through the next copy  brianna carson schmidt global news  hi there i think my question is for dr  you uh dr you i'm asking about the uh i  guess back sale for your  staff in order to fill these beds in  this new phone line we're hearing that  uh corporate or out of scope staff will  be taking on some other duties uh can  you talk about that and then i guess for  the premier why aren't you  asking either other provinces or the  military to step in and also bring an  extra hand  yeah so in terms of the first part of  the question absolutely anybody who has  any clinical experience  no matter what position they work in  within the organization we're actually  asking for their skill sets  what they've done in the past and  finding appropriate redeployment  positions for them i just want to say  thank you to our teams who have been  redeployed  for over two years and just to say it's  very difficult  to be redeployed into areas where you're  not familiar with and  you know our teams have just continued  to go above and beyond the call of duty  all the time when it comes to staffing  so i just second part of the question um  which was  why have i not called upon the canadian  military or other provinces to help us  out  well the answer is  that every province is stretched in  right now for exactly the same reasons  in fact alberta  has a lower uh per capita rate of  hospitalization from covet 19 than  canada as a whole and much lower than  for example uh ontario and quebec  so uh other provinces do not have spare  capacity  they're all stretched as as has every  part of the world i mean even the us  which spends a lot more  on health care and has uh relatively  more health care workers per capita uh  even many of their hospital systems have  been stretched for the same reasons  um and in terms of the canadian armed  forces the canadian armed forces as i've  pointed out before has extremely limited  um health  capacity they don't actually run a  hospital system anymore that ended about  25 years back  and when we did call on the uh forces  through the federal government for some  help back in  september for delta  they were able i think my recollection  was to provide nine  nurses  which  which helped us to maybe staff one or  two beds  in icu so  um and though and those assets have been  those individuals have been redeployed  to provinces that are harder hit so the  feds with their very limited health care  assets have to go to where the needs are  greatest i think right now that would be  quebec  which despite its curfew and lockdown  policies has been hardest hit province  in canada from omicron  thank you premier operator can you  please put through our final color  thank you audrey nimble radio canada  hi thank you for taking my question i'll  just start with a question in french on  something you've already been asked on  the this way  because  [Music]  [Music]  uh  thank you premier and audrey do you have  a follow-up  uh yes  was it oh  thank you everyone that concludes  today's press conference
 

